# claude.patterns — Claude Code CLI output patterns

IDLE_PATTERN='❯\s*$|^\$ $'
# NOTE (#17): the `❯` input box is drawn continuously, including mid-turn, so
# the classifier only trusts it when no working evidence is fresh. The real
# working discriminator is the status-row hint `esc to interrupt`, present
# while working and absent at rest. Dead spinner glyphs (◐◑◒◓◉◎○) were removed:
# they never appear (Claude cycles ✻ ✶ ✽ ✢ · *), and those glyphs CANNOT be
# used instead because Claude reuses them in completed-turn summaries
# ("✻ Brewed for 9m 52s"), which would mark finished turns as working.
# `● Read|● Write|…` were removed as unreachable: TOOL_START_PATTERN matches
# the same lines first and returns before the state machine.
WORKING_PATTERNS='esc to interrupt|● Working|↳ '
RATE_LIMIT_PATTERN='out of extra usage|Claude usage limit|monthly limit|quota exhausted|rate limit reached'
LOGIN_PATTERN='anthropic\.com/login|Please log in|authentication required'
TRUST_DIALOG_PATTERN='Do you trust the files'
BYPASS_PATTERN='bypass permissions on'
TOOL_START_PATTERN='● (Read|Write|Edit|Bash|Agent|WebSearch|WebFetch|Skill|Workflow|NotebookEdit)'
TOOL_END_PATTERN='✓ (Read|Write|Edit|Bash|Agent|WebSearch|WebFetch|Skill|Workflow|NotebookEdit).*\([0-9]'
ERROR_PATTERN='^\s*Error:|^\s*error:|^\s*FATAL|^\s*panic:|InputValidationError'
MODEL_PATTERN='model.*claude-|Switched to .*claude-'
SESSION_END_PATTERN='Session ended|Goodbye'
